        The SELL-SIDE PSA path, for the Disposition_PSA record type.
        Four steps: Initial Draft -> Revised -> Ready for Execution -> Executed.

        THE VALUES ARE IDENTICAL TO THE ACQUISITION PATH; ONLY THE WORDING DIFFERS, AND THAT IS
        THE WHOLE POINT OF THIS FILE. Unlike LOI__c and NDA__c, the PSA needed no new picklist
        values at all - the client document's four sell-side states are already exactly
        Initial Draft / Revised / Ready for Execution / Executed. What inverts is WHO ACTS:

          - OUR legal issues the FIRST DRAFT on a sale. On a purchase we receive the seller's
            paper and redline it. That inversion is the reason this file exists.
          - The counterparty is the BUYER, so Ball In Court reads Us / Buyer here and
            Us / Seller on the acquisition type.
          - Execution hands off to CLOSING on the Disposition, not to the Transactions team on
            an Opportunity.

        ⚠ THE 'Executed' STEP DELIBERATELY DOES NOT PROMISE AUTOMATION. The acquisition step
        says the Opportunity is stamped and the Transaction created, because that is built and
        live. The equivalent sell-side behaviour - moving Disposition_Stage__c to 'Closing' - is
        an APEX branch in ContractExecutionService that is NOT part of 3C and is not built yet.
        The wording therefore tells the user what should now be true and asks them to confirm
        it, which is honest whether or not the branch has shipped, and does not have to be
        rewritten when it does. Do not "upgrade" this text to assert automation until that
        branch is deployed and verified.

        NO AMPERSAND ENTITIES ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE - "purchase and sale agreement" is written
        out. The master path carries `&amp;amp;amp;` in its first step and whether that renders as an
        ampersand or literally has never been confirmed in this repo; the acquisition path
        reproduces it byte-identically under the do-not-reword rule, and this new file simply
        avoids inheriting the question.

        ⚠ DRIVEN BY Negotiation_Status__c, NOT Stage__c - the same constraint as the acquisition
        path and the same reason. Stage__c is a DERIVED PROJECTION recomputed by
        Contract_Review_Stage_Sync on every save, and a direct write to it commits and is
        silently discarded. 'Revised' and 'Ready for Execution' both project onto 'Review', so a
        Stage__c Path would sit still through one of the Advance Stage clicks. The disposition
        PSA must drive Negotiation_Status__c, never Stage__c.

        STEP ORDER COMES FROM THE PICKLIST, NOT FROM THIS FILE, and needed no adjustment: both
        record types expose the same four values in the master ordering, so nothing had to be
        appended or re-sequenced. Contrast NDA__c, where 'Not Sent' had to be moved AHEAD of
        'Sent' because the two sets overlap and appending rendered the disposition starting
        state third.

